{{also|hub-bub}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|whobub||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Mid 16th c. Perhaps from {{bor|en|ga|-}}; compare {{m+|ga|ababú}}!, {{m|ga|abú}}! (battle-cry), {{cog|gd|ub|ub! ub!}} (expressing contempt, etc.), {{m|gd|ubh ubh}}! (expressing disgust).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhʌbʌb/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hubbub.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[confuse]]d [[uproar]], [[commotion]], [[tumult]] or [[racket]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:commotion}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=2|passage=At length a universal '''hubbub''' wild<br>Of stunning sounds and voices all confused,<br>Borne through the hollow dark, assaults his ear<br>With loudest vehemence.|year=1873}}
#* {{quote-av|en|date=1943 October 30|title=w:Falling Hare|speaker=w:Bugs Bunny|passage=What's all the hubbub, bub?}}

